{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as stated in the amendment adopted on 2 May 2026[[cite:obs-0fea77438fbfe3945c0fd4e4af8f4005c2b0c0b2 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]]. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies[[cite:obs-0fea77438fbfe3945c0fd4e4af8f4005c2b0c0b2 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]].\n","expected_sha256":"9fbc345755650a9a623d20c2093d125a167cb8ac6150fc56b54e24d30b82056d","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Removed the statement about one half quorum from bylaws as it conflicts with the amendment and is forbidden. Kept only the amendment's quorum and the rule that amendment applies when differing, both supported by the amendment source."}